Description: GtkGLArea: stereo on X11, a child window declared as stereo content
 On X11 a stereo area is a child window of the toplevel's X window (a frame
 of the size of one view and, inside it, a window twice as wide), declared as
 full side by side stereo content and listed as the toplevel's stereo child
 with libstereo-declare (loaded with g_module when the first stereo area
 asks, so GTK has no dependency on it). The two views are read back and put
 into the window; the first frames are repeated because the window manager
 redirects the declared child a little after the declaration. An area that
 cannot do it (no library, a window manager that announces less than version
 8) says so with stereo-error and draws its left view alone, as on Wayland.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: other, Sparky Stereo OS
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-11-08
